# Testing Standards

## Priority behaviors (must have tests)

- `expiryDate` must be after `issuedDate`
- Status transitions: active ↔ expiring ↔ expired; renewal → `renewed`; delete → `archived`
- Status recalculation on date PATCH (Asia/Colombo)
- Expiry job idempotency (rerun does not double-update or duplicate events)
- Dashboard aggregation excludes renewed/archived
- Soft delete and employee cascade

## Conventions

| Module | Location | Naming |
|---|---|---|
| NestJS unit | beside module or `test/` | `*.spec.ts` |
| NestJS e2e | `backend/test/` | `*.e2e-spec.ts` |
| Python | `expiry-job/tests/` | `test_*.py` |
| Frontend | `src/lib/**/*.test.ts` | Vitest |

## Practices

- One behavior per test; descriptive test names
- Mock external I/O (HTTP, EventBridge, DB where unit-testing services)
- Use fixed dates for timezone-sensitive tests (`Asia/Colombo`)
- Add regression test for every bug fix
- Don't test framework boilerplate or trivial getters

## Before merge

- New features include tests for happy path and key edge cases
- Existing tests still pass (`npm run test`, `python -m pytest`)
